<section class="film film-seven" id="seven">
  <div class="film-bg-glow"></div>
  <div class="film-inner">
    <div class="film-poster-wrap reveal">
      <div class="poster-frame">
        <span class="year-tag">1995</span>
        <img src="http://www.impawards.com/1995/posters/seven_ver1.jpg" alt="Se7en movie poster" loading="lazy"/>
        <div class="rating"><span class="rating-stars">★★★★★</span><span class="rating-num">8.6</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="poster-caption">Dir. David Fincher · New Line Cinema · 1801×2815px</p>
    </div>
    <div class="film-text">
      <span class="film-label reveal">Film Two · Psychological Thriller</span>
      <h2 class="film-title reveal"><em>SE7EN</em></h2>
      <p class="film-director reveal">Directed by David Fincher</p>
      <p class="film-synopsis reveal">Two detectives — one jaded and days from retirement, one bright-eyed and newly arrived — hunt a serial killer whose murders each enact one of the seven deadly sins. Fincher builds a city that feels diseased, perpetually wet, where darkness isn't atmosphere but fact.</p>
      <p class="film-synopsis reveal">Se7en is a masterclass in controlled dread. It doesn't shock you — it slowly, methodically convinces you that the world is exactly as bad as you feared. The ending is among the most devastating in cinema history. You already know it. It still destroys you.</p>
      <div class="film-quote reveal">"Ernest Hemingway once wrote, 'The world is a fine place and worth fighting for.' I agree with the second part."</div>
      <div class="film-pills reveal">
        <span class="pill">Brad Pitt</span><span class="pill">Morgan Freeman</span>
        <span class="pill">Kevin Spacey</span><span class="pill">127 min</span>
      </div>
      <div class="film-credits reveal reveal-late">
        <div class="credit"><span class="credit-label">Director</span><span class="credit-val">David Fincher</span></div>
        <div class="credit"><span class="credit-label">Screenplay</span><span class="credit-val">Andrew Kevin Walker</span></div>
        <div class="credit"><span class="credit-label">Cinematography</span><span class="credit-val">Darius Khondji</span></div>
        <div class="credit"><span class="credit-label">Music</span><span class="credit-val">Howard Shore</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

